<p>Seeking Greenlights: Yes<br />
Page Type: SCP Article</p>
<p>Genre: Weird Tales</p>
<p>Page Layout: N/A</p>
<p>Elevator Pitch: A Discman plays exactly what needs to be heard; sometimes more than one bargains for.</p>
<p>Central Narrative:<br />
This article describes a portable cd-player identical to a Sony “Discman” of late 1980s manufacture, with the following qualities:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<ol>
<li>The brand name “Turing” rather than &quot;Sony.&quot; Rechargeable batteries found with the item are identical to Energizer “AA” batteries but are branded &quot;Integrity.&quot;</li>
<li>The item can be powered only with an included power adapter or with two (2) of four “Integrity” batteries.</li>
<li>The item appears to contain a cd; cannot be opened.</li>
<li>When activated, listener hears new, and original material created by their favorite musical performer OR a favorite comedian. (This seems to depend upon the “need” of the listener: do they need a laugh, or do they need to listen to mood appropriate music?)</li>
<li>Material theoretically produced by any individual who has recorded speech or performance from the time of Thomas Edison’s first intentional recording (“Mary Had a Little Lamb”) through the present. The living or dead status of an artist does not matter, but material is broadly contemporary. Robin Williams might have an entire routine about the current US political situation, but Benny Goodman isn’t going to perform a big band song about the Gulf War.</li>
<li>Material cannot be replicated or recorded. Efforts to sketch out compositions invariably fail. Jokes just fall apart. However, should subject actively express a desire to listen to a “recording” again. The recording may even be accessed by multiple people aware of its existence.</li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Hook/Attention-Grabber: This can of course be incredibly restorative, but the downside is that individuals who are exposed to use for a long period of time seem to become rather jealous of the material. Like children squabbling over a new video game or toy, adults will break into heated, sometimes violent, arguments when they wish to access the material and cannot do so. This effect is quickly apparent when more than one individual listens at a time.<br />
Additional Notes: Foundation would allow any Level 2+ staff to use the item within a controlled recreation area, with the following rules.</p>
<ol>
<li>Access limited to 1 use per week, up to 1 hour per listen, 1 staff per use.</li>
<li>Access provided via random lottery. No weight given to rank or experience.</li>
</ol>

